# Own-wording Tome of Heroes mundane goods (gear, tools, poisons, bombs, mounts, vehicles, clockwork creations, materials).
ITEMS = []; SP = {}; WPN = {}
MASTERY = {}
WDESC = {}
GEAR = []    # [name, cost gp, weight, type, text]

_CC = "Clockwork creation. "
_BOMB = "Bombs are explosive devices of many styles that all use gunpowder, so they have the gunpowder weapon property. As an action, light and throw one up to 20 feet so it shatters on impact. Make a ranged attack against a creature or object, treating it as an improvised weapon. On a hit the target takes damage and any extra effect for the bomb type. "
_GP = "Black powder is a granular alchemical mix of sulfur, charcoal and saltpeter, and a key part of bombs and the paper cartridges that firearms use. An ounce that you ignite burns for 1 round, shedding bright light in a 20-foot radius and dim light for 20 feet more. Larger amounts are far more dangerous, and used as a weapon or explosive it has the gunpowder weapon property. "
_EB = "As an action, throw this bottle up to 20 feet so it shatters on impact. Make a ranged attack against a creature or object, treating the bottle as an improvised weapon. On a hit the target takes damage and any extra effect by liquid type. "
_MANT = "A portable miniature wall of wood or wicker, shaped like a U or L, that shelters those behind it. It may have spikes to plant in the ground or wheels to roll. You can move and set one as part of your movement, but you move at half Speed. A damaged one that is not destroyed can be repaired during a rest if you have woodcarver's tools. "

GEAR += [
 ["Additional Control Rod", 1000, 0, "Other", _CC + "Modification. A clockwork crafter can make a duplicate of a creation's control rod so another creature can command it. If the creation gets conflicting commands from rod holders, it obeys the holder of the original rod. At the GM's option, counterfeit rods can imitate the rods of other creations, with a 25 percent chance of failing when used. On a roll of 1 the command fails and the creation spends its next turn attacking the counterfeit holder."],
 ["Additional Language", 500, 0, "Other", _CC + "Modification. Extra language gears let the creation understand another language. They can be hard to find, and the GM may rule that rare or exotic languages are unavailable. The gears enlarge the internal works, leaving a visible bulge in the head or chest. It grants understanding and speech only, so a creation that cannot speak still cannot speak the new language. Take it more than once for a different language each time."],
 ["Alchemical Bolt", 0.2, 0.1, "Ammunition", "A bulb-headed crossbow bolt. As an action, fill it with an alchemical liquid such as alchemist's fire or holy water. When it hits, it deals normal damage, then shatters and spills the liquid, subjecting the target to that substance."],
 ["Alchemical Bolts (5)", 1, 0.5, "Ammunition", "Five bulb-headed crossbow bolts. As an action, fill one with an alchemical liquid such as alchemist's fire or holy water. When it hits, it deals normal damage, then shatters and spills the liquid, subjecting the target to that substance."],
 ["Armor", 150, 0, "Other", _CC + "Modification. Iron plates bolted onto the creation raise its AC by 1, but they are heavy and awkward, reducing its Speed by 10 feet and giving it Disadvantage on Stealth checks. It cannot also have the Speed Boost modification."],
 ["Assassin Snake", 200, 0, "Other", _CC + "Sold as pest control. It crawls through walls or deep into burrows to remove nuisance pests. It has the Chemical Reservoir modification and comes preloaded with a basic poison vial or a flask of alchemist's fire, buyer's choice."],
 ["Bandolier", 0.1, 0, "Adventuring Gear", "A leather cross-body belt with loops and small pockets. It holds up to 20 paper cartridges and up to 3 pistols."],
 ["Bee Venom", 350, 0, "Adventuring Gear", "Poison harvested from living giant honey bees. A creature subjected to it makes a DC 15 Constitution save or takes 3d6 Poison damage and is Poisoned for 1 minute. While Poisoned this way it is also Paralyzed, and it repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success."],
 ["Beekeeper's Tools", 50, 10, "Tools", "Used to set up, tend and harvest beehives, which yield wax, venom and honey. The set has protective gear, a smoker, hive tools, a bee brush and extraction equipment. With proficiency, add your Proficiency Bonus to Nature checks about flowers and stinging insects, Animal Handling checks about bees, and Medicine checks about venom. Spend at least 1 hour a day on a hive to harvest 2 pounds of honey a week."],
 ["Camel Saddle", 60, 40, "Adventuring Gear", "Camels are the best mounts for desert travel. A well-fitted camel saddle lets you ride comfortably on the hump."],
 ["Canoe", 30, 50, "Vehicle", "A narrow rowed boat, about 16 feet long, holding up to two Medium creatures. Going downstream, add the current's speed, usually 3 miles per hour."],
 ["Cartridge Pouch", 1, 1, "Adventuring Gear", "A leather belt pouch holding 30 paper cartridges. It is coated with a retardant and has Resistance to Fire damage."],
 ["Cavalry Camel", 200, 0, "Other", "A combat-trained desert mount, aggressive to others but loyal to its master. It is as much a weapon as a steed and fights to the death to protect a dismounted rider. Usually a one-humped dromedary, though two-humped camels also appear on desert battlefields."],
 ["Chandler's Tools", 20, 6, "Tools", "Used to make candles from beeswax and other materials. The set has storage containers, wicks, molds, essential oils and a cauldron. With proficiency, add your Proficiency Bonus to Nature checks about wax, soaps, oils and similar materials, Religion checks about religious rituals, and Survival checks about starting, stopping or controlling nonmagical fires. With the right materials you can make 100 tapered candles a week."],
 ["Chemical Reservoir", 500, 0, "Other", _CC + "Modification. A reservoir holding one use of an alchemical substance, such as alchemist's fire or a dose of poison. The creation can empty it onto a creature it hits with a melee attack, subjecting the target to the substance if it could normally affect a creature hit by or touching it. The creation is not affected when it empties the reservoir, but can still be hurt by outside alchemical substances. Refilling takes 1 minute and one vial or dose. It cannot also have the Hidden Compartment modification."],
 ["Clockwork Gardener", 150, 0, "Other", _CC + "A tree-like creation with a bronze trunk and patina-coated copper leaves that blends into decorative gardens. It plants seeds, trims grass with scythe blades stored inside, and waters plants from a spigot and holes in its branches. Its pipes hold 10 gallons, which it can sprinkle under its branches or release in a burst. Its trunk has the Hidden Compartment modification, usually holding garden tools and supplies."],
 ["Clockwork Kestrel", 250, 0, "Other", _CC + "A tiny, gleaming brass and copper bird with jewel eyes that click with each blink, emitting a faint whir and whisper of steam. It has two Recounting Crystal modifications as eyes that record sound as well as sight, up to 4 hours each instead of 1. A recorded sound is projected as an illusion like minor illusion. It can have no other modifications except Familiar."],
 ["Clockwork Lantern", 100, 0, "Other", _CC + "An upgraded hooded lantern that floats up to 10 feet off the ground and follows a creature holding or carrying its control rod. On command it adjusts its wick to shed bright light in a 5 to 30 foot radius and dim light for the same distance beyond, and can snuff or light itself. It has the Chemical Reservoir modification, but only for lantern oil. Once lit it burns 6 hours on a flask of oil. It can also lob small tongues of fire a short distance to deter predators or light campfires."],
 ["Clockwork Tutor", 1000, 0, "Other", _CC + "It studies a creature holding or carrying its control rod and learns how that creature learns. When that creature is learning a language or tool proficiency, the tutor cannot be the instructor but helps, cutting the downtime days needed by 25 percent. It does not need to know the language or the tool."],
 ["Clockwork Warhorse", 500, 0, "Other", _CC + "A tireless mechanical destrier that needs no food, favored by gearforged who find living mounts finicky. It is bulkier and slower than a living warhorse. It needs basic maintenance each week, 1 hour of work and 1 gp of materials, and no tools. Its control is a set of reins built into its head and neck rather than a rod. If it has more than one control rod, as with Additional Control Rod, it obeys the holder of its reins first."],
 ["Dark Dream", 250, 0, "Adventuring Gear", "A gas distilled from a rare underground fungus with necrotic energy, made and favored by the derro. It puts creatures other than derro to sleep. As an action, unseal the glass bottle or throw it up to 20 feet to shatter it. Each breathing creature within 10 feet makes a DC 13 Constitution save or is Poisoned for 1 hour and Unconscious while so. It repeats the save at the end of each minute, ending the effect on a success. It wakes if it takes damage or another creature uses an action to shake it awake."],
 ["Elemental Bottle", 0, 1, "Adventuring Gear", _EB + "Acid, cold, fire, lightning, poison and thunder versions exist, each listed separately."],
 ["Elemental Bottle (Acid)", 25, 1, "Adventuring Gear", _EB + "**Acid.** A target hit takes 2d6 Acid damage."],
 ["Elemental Bottle (Cold)", 50, 1, "Adventuring Gear", _EB + "**Cold.** A target hit takes 1d4 Cold damage and its Speed is halved for 1 minute. At the end of each of its turns it can make a DC 10 Constitution save to end the effect."],
 ["Elemental Bottle (Fire)", 50, 1, "Adventuring Gear", _EB + "**Fire.** A target hit takes 1d4 Fire damage and catches fire. Until a creature uses an action to douse it, the target takes 1d4 Fire damage at the start of each of its turns."],
 ["Elemental Bottle (Lightning)", 100, 1, "Adventuring Gear", _EB + "**Lightning.** A target hit takes 1d6 Lightning damage and makes a DC 10 Constitution save or is Paralyzed until the end of its next turn."],
 ["Elemental Bottle (Poison)", 100, 1, "Adventuring Gear", _EB + "**Poison.** A target hit takes 1d4 Poison damage and is Poisoned for 1 minute. At the end of each of its turns it can make a DC 10 Constitution save to end the condition."],
 ["Elemental Bottle (Thunder)", 75, 1, "Adventuring Gear", _EB + "**Thunder.** A target hit takes 1d4 Thunder damage and is Deafened for 1 minute. At the end of each of its turns it can make a DC 10 Constitution save to end the condition."],
 ["Elephant Saddle", 150, 90, "Adventuring Gear", "Elephants are fearsome war beasts but tiring to ride for long. An elephant saddle looks like a wide chair with a low back and armrests."],
 ["Elven Adaptive Leaves", 100, 3, "Adventuring Gear", "Adhesive leather leaves dyed green, brown and gray. They cover one suit of armor or set of clothing for a Medium or smaller creature, or one shield, for 24 hours, and take 10 minutes to apply. While you wear or wield something covered with them, you have Advantage on Stealth checks to hide in a forest or other heavily vegetated terrain. When the time ends, the leaves fall off one by one and cannot be reused."],
 ["Elven Spellbook", 75, 4, "Adventuring Gear", "A tome bound in wood wrapped in treated leaves, with 120 pages of papyrus for recording spells. Its pages include reference pages, marked pages and pages folded in unique shapes, which feel natural to wizards despite the odd order. The time to prepare wizard spells from it is halved."],
 ["Expanded Reservoir", 250, 0, "Other", _CC + "Modification. The creation must have a Chemical Reservoir. This enlarges the reservoir, which stays one container, so all doses must be the same poison or substance. Maximum doses by size are 2 (Tiny), 3 (Small), 5 (Medium) or 7 (Large). Instead of emptying the reservoir when it hits with a melee attack, the creation releases one dose. Refilling takes 1 minute and the right number of doses."],
 ["Familiar", 200, 0, "Other", _CC + "Modification, only for the assassin snake, clockwork kestrel, clockwork lantern or watch owl. The creation can serve a spellcaster as a familiar. To add it, the spellcaster and creation spend at least 4 hours each day in a ritual led by the clockwork crafter, during which the caster absorbs the control rod's power and the rod breaks. After that the two share a magic telepathic bond. While within 1 mile of each other, the caster senses what the creation senses. While the creation is within 10 feet, the caster shares its Magic Resistance trait. If the creation is damaged but not destroyed, the caster can pay half its price to repair it, keeping the bond. If it is destroyed, the bond ends."],
 ["Fireorb Bomb", 100, 0.5, "Explosive", _BOMB + "**Fireorb.** Ornate engraved metal spheres favored by dwarves. On a hit, the target takes 1d4 Piercing plus 1d6 Fire damage, and each creature within 5 feet of it makes a DC 12 Dexterity save or takes 1d6 Fire damage."],
 ["Gardener's Tools", 8, 10, "Tools", "All the equipment to dig and till soil by hand, plant seeds, transplant crops, gather clippings and pull weeds."],
 ["Ghoul Saliva Paste", 100, 0, "Adventuring Gear", "A pungent mash of meat and tissue pre-chewed by ghouls and soaked in their saliva. Unscrupulous people and some darakhul hunters coat weapons with it to disable targets briefly. A creature subjected to it makes a DC 10 Constitution save or is Paralyzed for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns to end it. Holding ammunition or a weapon coated with it gives you Disadvantage on Stealth checks against creatures with the Keen Smell trait."],
 ["Glidecloak", 200, 2, "Adventuring Gear", "A finely woven cloak with loops at the sides and bottom for your hands and feet, making a wing-like surface. While you wear it and fall, you can use an action each turn to glide horizontally half your falling speed in a direction you choose. If you succeed on a DC 15 Acrobatics check before hitting the ground, you land without falling damage. It does nothing if you fall less than 15 feet."],
 ["Grappling Rod", 200, 10, "Adventuring Gear", "A wooden rod with a miniature grappling hook in its hollow, attached to a drum holding 100 feet of strong rope. Two buttons run the clockwork inside. As an action, press one to launch the hook at a point you can see within 100 feet, where it catches on a ledge, rock, battlement or other protrusion. You can also launch at an unseen but obvious spot, such as a leafy branch or a ledge lip above you. The GM may require an attack roll or Dexterity check at some spots, such as narrow battlements or steep roofs, or rule that they lack anything to catch on. As a bonus action, press the second button to retract the rope at 50 feet per round. If the hook is secured and you hold the rod, you and what you wear or carry are pulled toward the hook at that speed. It holds up to 500 pounds."],
 ["Gu", 1800, 0, "Adventuring Gear", "Poison distilled from the combined venom of vipers, centipedes, scorpions, toads and spiders. Properly made, it has no taste or odor. A creature that ingests it feels nothing for 1d4 days. Any effect that ends the Poisoned condition removes it from the body. If it is still present when time runs out, the creature's organs swell and burst, and it makes a DC 19 Constitution save, taking 10d10 Poison damage on a failure or half on a success."],
 ["Gunpowder", 0.1, 0.0625, "Explosive", _GP + "This entry is one ounce."],
 ["Gunpowder (Barrel)", 125, 100, "Explosive", _GP + "A barrel holds about 40 horns. Igniting a full barrel makes it explode at the end of the next round. Each creature within 15 feet makes a DC 12 Dexterity save, taking 2d4 Piercing plus 5d6 Fire damage on a failure or half on a success."],
 ["Gunpowder (Horn)", 3, 1, "Explosive", _GP + "A horn holds enough for 30 paper cartridges. Igniting a full horn makes it explode at once. Each creature within 5 feet makes a DC 12 Dexterity save, taking 2d6 Fire damage on a failure or half on a success."],
 ["Gunpowder (Keg)", 65, 50, "Explosive", _GP + "A keg holds about 20 horns. Igniting a full keg makes it explode at the end of the next round. Each creature within 10 feet makes a DC 12 Dexterity save, taking 1d4 Piercing plus 3d6 Fire damage on a failure or half on a success."],
 ["Gunsmith's Tools", 50, 8, "Tools", "Calipers, files, hammers, iron pin punches, pliers and a cleaning kit. With proficiency, add your Proficiency Bonus to ability checks to analyze, repair or craft firearms."],
 ["Handheld Bomb", 60, 1, "Explosive", _BOMB + "**Handheld.** The most common small bombs. On a hit they deal 1d6 Fire damage."],
 ["Heavy Large Mantlet", 100, 100, "Adventuring Gear", _MANT + "This large wooden one has three wheels and shelters many creatures on a battlefield, letting soldiers gain ground steadily. It covers up to two Medium or smaller creatures or one Large creature, who have Cover from attacks from the far side. It has 25 hit points, AC 15 and a damage threshold of 5."],
 ["Heavy Personal Mantlet", 50, 50, "Adventuring Gear", _MANT + "This wooden one has three wheels and is much heavier than the wicker kind. It cannot be folded but protects better. A Medium or smaller creature behind it has Cover from attacks from the far side. It has 20 hit points, AC 15 and a damage threshold of 2."],
 ["Hidden Compartment", 50, 0, "Other", _CC + "Modification. A concealed compartment found with a DC 13 Investigation check. Capacity by size is 1/5 cubic foot (Tiny), 1 (Small), 2 (Medium) or 3 (Large). It cannot also have the Chemical Reservoir modification."],
 ["Homing Pigeon", 10, 0, "Other", "A tiny two-tone gray bird with black speckled wings, black bands on its body, an intelligent gaze, and a faint metallic sheen on its small neck feathers. Field commanders have long used them to send messages home. It does not take commands from designated humanoids. Instead it can be trained to remember particular humanoids or places and deliver messages to them with its Messenger trait. Any humanoid can attach a message and send it to a remembered target. It can remember up to three, and each takes a week of training with that humanoid or at that place. Training a fourth makes it forget the one it has gone longest without visiting."],
 ["Insectbane Candle", 1, 0, "Adventuring Gear", "A heavily scented candle that repels insects. While it burns, nonmagical insects stay out of a 5-foot radius around it. It burns 1 hour and sheds bright light in a 5-foot radius and dim light for 5 feet more."],
 ["Karaskara Powder", 600, 0, "Adventuring Gear", "Snake branch tree seeds ground into a silvery powder that causes great pain and violent convulsions when inhaled. A creature subjected to it makes a DC 13 Constitution save or takes 3d6 Poison damage and is Incapacitated for 1 minute. While Incapacitated it takes 1d6 Poison damage at the start of each of its turns, and it repeats the save at the end of each turn, ending the effect after three successes."],
 ["Kite Shield", 15, 10, "Adventuring Gear", "A shield favored by mounted warriors, shaped to guard the rider's legs and the mount's flank. It gives +2 AC. When you use it while mounted, the bonus applies to your mount's AC as well as yours."],
 ["Light Personal Mantlet", 25, 15, "Adventuring Gear", _MANT + "This wicker one has spikes to plant in the ground and folds to carry in a backpack or sling over a shoulder, folding or unfolding as an action. A Medium or smaller creature behind it has Cover from attacks from the far side. It has 15 hit points and AC 13."],
 ["Maddening Blindness", 500, 0, "Adventuring Gear", "A poison paste of crushed spores from bioluminescent fungi. A creature subjected to it makes a DC 15 Constitution save or is Blinded for 1d4 hours. The poison lingers after sight returns and gives nightmares at the next rest. The creature repeats the save when it finishes its next rest, and on a failure gains only the benefits of a short rest instead."],
 ["Magazine, Clockwork Crossbow", 0.5, 0.5, "Ammunition", "A feeding magazine for the clockwork crossbow."],
 ["Magazine, Dwarven Revolving Musket", 1, 1, "Ammunition", "A feeding magazine for the dwarven revolving musket."],
 ["Manica", 6, 4, "Adventuring Gear", "A shield of overlapping metal segments strapped to the upper and lower arm. You can don or doff it as an action. It gives +1 AC, less than other shields, but leaves your shield hand free. You cannot gain its bonus while wielding a weapon in that hand, and as usual you gain the benefit of only one shield."],
 ["Megaraptor", 800, 0, "Other", "Prehistoric titans still walk the hidden jungles. Nearly thirty feet long yet fast, agile and light at about 1 ton, a megaraptor has a foot-long scythe claw on each forelimb rather than the sickle foot claws of other raptors. Some jungle tribes know how to raise and train them as mounts and war beasts."],
 ["Memory Sphere", 300, 0.5, "Adventuring Gear", "A living crystal globe made by specially bred, long-lived insects as a keepsake for near-immortal elves. It holds one small item no bigger than a coin, key, ring or medallion. As an action, insert or remove an item from the self-sealing sphere. When you insert one, you can whisper a phrase of 10 words or fewer to the insect, and rubbing its belly makes it repeat the phrase in your voice. At the GM's option, hearing it can help you recall related information, giving Advantage on the check."],
 ["Mining Bomb", 150, 10, "Explosive", _BOMB + "**Mining.** Miners use these to clear stone and ore, and they also work against structures and foundations. These heavy bombs must be placed and lit, not thrown. After you light the fuse, it explodes at the end of your next turn. Each creature within 10 feet makes a DC 12 Dexterity save, taking 2d6 Fire damage on a failure or half on a success. An unworn, uncarried nonmagical object or structure in the area takes 4d6 Fire damage instead."],
 ["Monkshood Resin", 400, 0, "Adventuring Gear", "A thick syrup extracted from monkshood petals. A creature subjected to it makes a DC 13 Constitution save or takes 4d6 Poison damage. If it fails by 5 or more, it also loses the use of one limb for 1 minute, with the GM choosing the limb and effect. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, regaining the limb on a success."],
 ["Oliphaunt Warbeast", 800, 0, "Other", "A huge pachyderm with four scimitar-like tusks, thick gray-brown hide with patches of coarse black hair, a short trunk above a toothy maw, and large drooping ears. Armies prize young trained ones for breaching enemy defenses."],
 ["Paper Cartridge", 0.2, 0.1, "Ammunition", "A small tube of beeswax-coated paper holding gunpowder and a metal bullet. It is the main ammunition for weapons with the gunpowder property."],
 ["Paper Cartridges (10)", 2, 1, "Ammunition", "Ten small tubes of beeswax-coated paper, each holding gunpowder and a metal bullet. They are the main ammunition for weapons with the gunpowder property."],
 ["Pit Terrier", 100, 0, "Other", "A low-slung, compact, muscular dog with short fur, short widespread legs, a big flat head with a strong underbite and sharp lower teeth. Bred for war, it is fiercely loyal and fights to the death to protect its master, yet in peacetime it is as friendly as any dog and a good pet."],
 ["Pygmy Woolly Rhinoceros", 200, 0, "Other", "A mastiff-sized pachyderm with shaggy brown, gray or black fur, found mainly in arctic lands. Curious and social, though aggressive if it or its young are threatened. As clever as a dog, it can be trained for battle or tricks like fetching and jumping. Some northern halflings and dwarves use them as mounts and pack beasts."],
 ["Recounting Crystal", 750, 0, "Other", _CC + "Modification. A small crystal, usually in the head, that lets the creation record up to 1 hour of what it sees. It starts or ends a recording as a bonus action. A creature holding the control rod can use an action to project a recording in a space within 5 feet of the creation, as an illusion like silent image. The recording is visual only. It keeps only 1 hour at a time. The rod holder can erase it, either the full hour or in 1-minute increments."],
 ["River Barge", 1500, 0, "Vehicle", "A wide, flat-bottomed boat built to carry crates and barrels of goods on a river, moved by barge poles. Its speed mostly follows the current, usually 3 miles per hour, added to its speed when going downstream. It has a crew of two and no room for passengers, and can be towed upstream by draft animals on the bank."],
 ["Sand Skimmer", 50, 50, "Vehicle", "A wooden land vehicle that slides over sand under a single sail. A flat platform 5 feet wide and 10 feet long rides on two narrow runners. One driver pilots it and it carries one passenger. It weighs 50 pounds and has a folding mast, so it can ride in a cart or wagon or be dragged on foot. In good wind it reaches 8 miles per hour."],
 ["Sapper Tar", 50, 1, "Alchemical", "A thick alchemical liquid that softens earth and stone. As an action, smear the jar onto a nonmagical object or structure of earth or stone, weakening up to a 1-foot cube of it for 1 minute. Its damage threshold drops by 5, and the stone turns pliable as firm clay, so you can carve symbols, pull shackles or hinges free, silently set a piton, and so on. Alternatively, as an action pour it on, or throw it up to 20 feet at, a construct or elemental of earth or stone within reach, shattering the jar. Make a ranged attack, treating the tar as an improvised weapon. On a hit the creature's AC drops by 2 for 1 minute, and at the end of each of its turns it can make a DC 12 Constitution save to end the effect."],
 ["Shadowmaker", 1000, 0, "Adventuring Gear", "A thin black oil taken from plants killed by necrotic damage or other supernatural blight. A creature subjected to it makes a DC 19 Constitution save or is Poisoned for 8 hours. While so, its Strength score drops by 1d3 at the end of each hour, and it then repeats the save, ending the poison on a success. It dies if Strength reaches 0, and a humanoid that dies this way rises 1d4 hours later as a shadow. Otherwise the loss lasts until it finishes a rest after the poison ends."],
 ["Silt Mask", 50, 0.5, "Adventuring Gear", "A covering that keeps sand and irritants out of the airway. The wearer has Advantage on saves against effects delivered by breathing. Casting a spell with a verbal component while wearing it needs a DC 10 Constitution check, and on a failure the spell slot is spent with no effect."],
 ["Slughide Dissolvent (Cylinder)", 350, 1.5, "Adventuring Gear", "A clear gel kept in a brass and crystal cylinder that sprays. As an action, press the plunger to spray a line 30 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each creature in it makes a DC 13 Dexterity save, taking 2d6 Acid damage on a failure or half on a success. A creature that failed takes 1d4 Acid damage at the start of each of its turns and can make a DC 13 Constitution save at the end of each to end it. Dousing it in a gallon of wine ends the effect at once. The cylinder cannot be used again until reloaded, which costs 75 gp."],
 ["Slughide Dissolvent (Sphere)", 75, 1, "Adventuring Gear", "A clear gel kept in a porcelain sphere. As an action, throw it up to 20 feet so it shatters on impact. Make a ranged attack against a creature or object, treating it as an improvised weapon. On a hit the target takes 1d6 Acid damage and is covered in acid, taking 1d4 Acid damage at the start of each of its turns. It can make a DC 13 Constitution save at the end of each to end it. Dousing it in a gallon of wine ends the effect at once."],
 ["Speed Boost", 150, 0, "Other", _CC + "Modification. Removing some armor plating raises the creation's Speed by 10 feet and lowers its AC by 1. It cannot also have the Armor modification."],
 ["Surgery Kit", 50, 4, "Adventuring Gear", "A leather roll fastened by a cord, holding scalpels, a whetstone, a small mirror, sponges, bandages, needles, a box of soap and a bobbin of strong silk thread. It works like a healer's kit and has 10 uses. If you spend a use treating an injured creature during a rest and it spends a Hit Die to regain hit points, any 1 or 2 it rolls counts as a 3. Replacing the consumables costs 25 gp."],
 ["Sweet Vengeance", 1500, 0, "Adventuring Gear", "A poison distilled slowly from a great deal of worker bee venom, tasting just like honey. A creature that ingests it makes a DC 17 Constitution save. On a failure by 5 or more it crystallizes and is instantly Petrified. On any other failure it starts turning to crystallized honey and is Restrained. It repeats the save at the end of its next turn, becoming Petrified on a failure or ending the effect on a success. The petrification lasts until greater restoration or similar magic frees it."],
 ["Trinket", 0, 0, "Other", "At character creation you can roll percentile dice once on the Trinkets table to find an oddity you found or inherited. Work it into your backstory, or with the GM decide how and why you have it. It may even be a mystery to you and your character. A GM can also use the table to stock shops, chests or pockets with small oddities."],
 ["Trip Sphere", 100, 1, "Explosive", "An apple-sized iron sphere holding gunpowder in an alchemical solution. As an action, throw it up to 30 feet. It detonates with concussive force on impact and is destroyed. Each creature within 5 feet of where it landed makes a DC 10 Dexterity save or is knocked Prone."],
 ["Upas Sap", 350, 0, "Adventuring Gear", "A rare poison harvested from deep-jungle vines. A creature subjected to it makes a DC 13 Constitution save or is Poisoned for 1 minute. While so, its throat swells, it is suffocating, and it cannot breathe, speak or cast spells with verbal components. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns to end the effect."],
 ["War Pig", 50, 0, "Other", "A muscular, human-sized swine with bristly brown and gray hair and long curved lower tusks, the bane of cavalry and other animal-using units. They are often untrained. Officers pen them in the dark and release them against the enemy just before their own army advances. Less scrupulous commanders douse them in pitch and set them alight. An incendiary war pig takes 1d6 Fire damage each round, and any creature that hits it with a melee attack takes 1d6 Fire damage."],
 ["War Wagon", 250, 0, "Vehicle", "A land vehicle for carrying armored fighters across battlefields, reinforced with metal bands and often decked with spikes, sturdy shields or symbols of the war party's cause. As a pulled vehicle, its speed depends on the horses, and it needs a team of at least two to move. Several can be circled into a quick fortification, and most have arrow slits. Creatures inside a wagon or wagon circle have Cover from attacks outside. It has 30 hit points, AC 17, a damage threshold of 5, and immunity to Poison and Psychic damage."],
 ["Watch Owl", 150, 0, "Other", _CC + "It watches an area and warns the creature holding its control rod of trespassers, by gentle hoots, a loud screech, or a mental alert as set. It must be within 100 feet of the rod holder to be told to keep watch, but can mentally alert the holder from up to 1 mile away. These owls come in silver, gold, or painted to look like a natural owl."],
 ["Wolverine", 50, 0, "Other", "A shaggy, low-slung animal that looks like a badger crossed with a grizzly bear, with a short broad muzzle full of small teeth and five long ragged claws on each paw. Some dwarven armies use them to tunnel under enemy holdings. Once they surface behind enemy lines, they act as shock troops and soften the enemy while the army moves through the tunnel."],
 ["Wormsilk Cloak", 200, 3, "Adventuring Gear", "A full, hooded cloak in vivid colors. When a creature you can see attacks you and you have a hand free, use a Reaction to pull the cloak between you. You gain Resistance to Piercing damage from nonmagical attacks until the start of your next turn. If the Piercing damage is from a critical hit, you still resist as normal, but the cloak is destroyed."],
 ["Wormsilk Rope", 20, 4, "Adventuring Gear", "Rope with 4 hit points that can be burst or detached with a DC 20 Strength check."],
 ["Cold Iron", 0, 0, "Other", "Special material. Fey are timeless and shrug off most threats except weapons of cold-wrought iron, which undoes the fabric of their life and blights their ageless flesh. Against fey, a cold iron weapon counts as magical, and it is the only weapon with a hope of harming the most powerful fey lords and ladies. Making one is hard, and the skill and material double its price or add 100 gp, whichever is more. A smith able to make a lasting weapon without fire is hard to find, and one with the nerve to anger the fey courts harder still."],
 ["Peachwood", 0, 0, "Other", "Special material. Wood of fragrant peach trees, used for weapons against the undead. For any other item it is no different from oak or pine. A peachwood weapon deals 1d4 Bludgeoning damage on a hit whatever its size or shape. When it hits an undead creature, though, it counts as a magic weapon and deals damage as the weapon type it resembles. A peachwood greatsword deals 1d4 Bludgeoning to a human but 2d6 Slashing to a ghost."],
 ["Soulbound Steel", 0, 0, "Other", "Special material. Steel forged with the prepared ashes of fallen dead makes a light gray alloy with a powdery finish, sometimes worked in frost-like patterns, said to hold a sliver of a warrior's spirit. It is used for weapons and rarely shields. A weapon of it costs 500 gp more, reflecting the material and the care needed to keep the sliver intact without weakening the weapon. When you make an Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma save while holding or carrying an item of soulbound steel, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on it. Once used, you cannot use this again until you finish a rest, and you can benefit only once per day no matter how many such items you have."],
 ["Wave-Washed Steel", 0, 0, "Other", "Special material. Iron, wood ash and a rare metal from deep within ancient mountains make a light, flexible, very strong steel with a wave-like pattern. It is used for weapons, never armor. A weapon of it costs 250 gp more, reflecting the rare metal and the expertise needed. Only weapons made mainly of metal qualify, so a longsword can be wave-washed but a quarterstaff cannot. When you score a critical hit with one against a creature wearing armor or with natural armor, the target's armor is damaged and takes a cumulative -1 penalty to the AC it gives. This lasts until crafted armor is repaired or the creature finishes a rest for natural armor. Such a weapon cannot lower a creature's AC below 10."],
 ["Windforged Steel", 0, 0, "Other", "Special material. Made only in clifftop forges, this very strong, lightweight steel is deep blue, almost black, never rusts, and survives blows and magical effects that would destroy lesser metals. It is made into weapons and shields but seldom armor. An item of it has Advantage on saves to resist being damaged or destroyed, and attacks against it have Disadvantage. It is immune to rust, including from rust monsters and similar creatures. It weighs 25 percent less and has twice the hit points of the same item in ordinary metal. An item of it costs 25 percent more than a standard one."],
]
